name: harness-blindspot
kind: inferred
shape: categorical
face: in
membrane: false
note: |
  Fires when a marker/status type is recognized by one part of the test
  harness (run_regression.sh / regression_lib.sh actually gating what runs, or
  generate-test-index.js's status vocabulary) but invisible to the ONE script
  that backs the published board (scripts/save-snapshot.js). A test opted out
  by the recognized half silently rots into 'untested' in the published half
  — no reason, still counted against the rate.

  Caught this once for BENCHMARK (420_PERFORMANCE/BENCHMARK swallowed 14 real
  MUST_RUN tests with zero record — 016_the_honest_board). The category-level
  SKIP path had the identical shape (a synthesised 'Category skipped' string
  instead of the authored reason in the SKIP file) even with no live instance
  to expose it.

  Value is the count of marker types with this recognized/unrecognized split
  across the three status-computing scripts (save-snapshot.js,
  generate-status.js's fallback, generate-test-index.js) at time of check.

  Detector: for each of TODO/SKIP/BROKEN/BENCHMARK, confirm all three scripts
  read it, propagate it category-wise the same way, and thread an authored
  reason rather than a synthesized placeholder.
